Z||000008||87GT||03-10-2000||12:14 AM||||Hey everyone, I have a question.  Is this fiero meet in Daytona for fiero club people only or can anybody and there fiero show up?  THanks. I live north of Tampa and may take a drive over there||||reg||1
Z||000009||Phil||03-10-2000||05:54 AM||||Open to everybody||||reg||1
Z||000010||Old Lar||03-10-2000||07:46 AM||||The show at Daytona is open to all.  Every make, model and type of car.  There may well be 1500-2000 cars at the show.  Lots of vendors for metal cars (not many Fiero vendors, Waynes World was there last year, as was Mr. Mike, Danny Patton and a few others. <P>There have been some nice Plymouth Super B's there in the past.  Those were the hot cars for me back in the 60's.  426 hemi powered car with a 4 foot wing on the back. The Dodge version (Dodge Daytona) was the first car to break the 200 mph speed at Daytona.  Not the street version, all those cars GTO's, Road runners, 409 Chevys, 429 Cylones, Mustangs etc, relativly inexpensive cars, young kids and insurance rates through the roof did away with them rather quickly.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><BR>All you young guys are paying the super high insurance rates for the "fast" Fieros now.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Spyder||03-10-2000||01:47 PM||||Ok, Here is a picture of me:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mindspring.com/~mm889-19/Mark.jpg"> <BR>The picture doesn’t show my Beer Belly.<BR>I will be wondering around Saturday morning and afternoon with a Cute Blond! (my wife)<BR>If you guys want to meet somewhere at the show at a certain time let me know.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Old Lar||03-10-2000||04:20 PM||||Spyder:  The last three years all the Fieros were grouped together on the infield to the left of the tunnel at Daytona.  It was all neatly arranged by Fiero year. Frank Martin and Greg Lee will have the low down at the Holiday Inn in Daytona Shores (host hotel.  All the Fiero fanatics will be there.<P>You won't have any difficulty seeing Fiero people, once you locate the Daytona Infield. I'll be the one in sun glasses  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||turbo86se||03-11-2000||11:09 AM||||I'm going to try to make it, I've been having problems with my 88 starting sometimes, computer? But I may be able to make it down there for two days. <BR>I met Greg Lee a couple years ago in N. Charleston. He's very nice and funny! His 88 coupe is sweet!!! If I don't see you there I will be in Williamsburg, PA in June for VA Fieros show. I will be driving the turbo!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
